<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE electron-hawkeye360 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Electron &#x27;We&#x27;re Not Hawking Around&#x27; (3x HawkEye 360) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Loft: Rocket Lab Electron Payload User Guide 8.0 example flight profile: altitude knots 0@0s, ~78km@155s, ~82km@162s, ~126km@184s; orbit reached (S2 cutoff) L+535s.
Source: https://rocketlabcorp.com/assets/Rocket-Lab-Electron-Payload-User-Guide-8.0.pdf
Guide publishes NO velocities and NO SECO altitude. Two explicit assumptions (beyond EOS-05&#x27;s one):
(a) SECO altitude set to the 520 km deployment orbit (Rocket Lab mission page), altitude linear 184s-&gt;535s;
(b) horizontal split: ground-relative horizontal speed ramps linearly 0 -&gt; 7.658 km/s (circular v at 520 km minus Earth-rotation along Az) at 535s.
Real Electron parks in a lower elliptical orbit and Kick Stage circularizes ~T+50 min; this file ends at S2 cutoff.
Az = 180 - asin(cos 97 / cos lat) = 189.06 deg (direct-launch southbound, i=97 deg SSO per Rocket Lab). Mission flown: LL2 Success.
Pad (LL2): -39.262833N 177.864469E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=189.06 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-10-23T07:11:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
